id: pm-ado-resolution-recovery-race
title: Investigate intermittent same-decision recovery writer failure under coverage load
description: "PR 91 serial release validation observed the unchanged test resolution recovery serializes two writers using the same prepared decision fail during the Bun V8 coverage suite. The same test passed in the earlier npm suite and passes a focused retry, so the underlying interleaving remains unresolved. This is separate from the fixture preload and closeout provenance review fixes. Preserve the original failure and do not weaken writer safety assertions to mask it."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: concurrency,recovery,testing
created_at: "2026-11-08T08:03:32.358Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T23:31:45.542Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Capture the exact failing assertion and refusal values; reproduce the relevant interleaving with real native trackers under coverage; determine whether production recovery or the acceptance oracle is wrong; preserve one remote PATCH, at least one accepted writer, deterministic replay and unchanged coverage thresholds."
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-08T08:15:13.251Z",codex-agent,"Final broad-suite failure detail: the assertion in test/sync.test.ts:1509 rejects the concurrent writer refusal because its code is outside ado_partial_apply/apply_failed. The reporter does not include the actual refusal code, so capture it during investigation rather than assuming a production or test-only cause. The test passed in the earlier npm V8 suite and its subsequent focused retry passes 1/1; the Bun broad suite failed it once. No safety assertion was relaxed. That suite was separately cancelled at the 1650-second local gate limit; cancellation and partial coverage are not this assertion failure."
  "2026-11-08T12:27:27.674Z",codex-agent,"PR 91 review PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860_Uoy: documented the TypeScript runtime prerequisite in the item body rather than rewriting historical evidence. The current continuation uses Node 24.19.0. Search of package retry records found this one focused retry entry; package engines already require Node 22.18+. Preserve the original command and name filter. The production concurrency investigation remains open."
  "2026-11-08T12:39:33.038Z",codex-agent,"Runtime documentation regression passes through the pinned pm test runner: 1/1, zero skipped/cancelled. Native-parser and package-wide deadline regression baseline passes 3/3; removing only this prerequisite body in a disposable package copy makes its documentation contract fail 0/1, and restoration passes. This resolves only review PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860_Uoy; the underlying intermittent same-decision writer observation remains an open investigation. No production recovery assertion or audit event changed."
  "2026-11-08T19:59:48.654Z",codex-agent,"PR 91 final review PRRT_kwDOUMUq1861CPxG: replaced both executable test links with double-quoted test-name patterns for POSIX shells and Windows cmd.exe. Historical comments and history bytes are unchanged; this adjusts current executable links only. The package-wide audit found and corrected the same pattern in four other linked commands. Production same-decision recovery investigation remains unresolved and this item will return to open without a claim."
  "2026-11-16T12:10:18.128Z",codex-sol,"Recurrence on caller pin PR #111, Bun release job 132763811635: test/sync.test.ts concurrent same-decision recovery rejects a code outside ado_partial_apply/apply_failed (assertion at line 1509); the runner log did not include the actual code. The workflow-only diff does not change recovery. Keep this unresolved and preserve one PATCH, accepted writer and replay assertions."
  "2026-11-24T20:32:59.384Z",codex-agent,"Scheduled run 45408908701 failed Run release checks. The V8 suite passed 1645 of 1646 tests, with this concurrent-writer assertion as the sole failure. The log does not print the losing refusal code. A focused retry passed, so the test needs a forced post-settlement interleaving."
  "2026-11-24T20:44:52.570Z",codex-agent,"Deterministic non-Git fixture pauses at Azure agreement read-back and lets the peer replay the same settled decision before the first writer checks its native fence. Reverting only resolution.ts returns stale_local (0 of 1), matching the rejection class excluded by the hosted test. With the fix, matching peer agreement yields retryable ado_partial_apply, with one PATCH and byte-stable replay. The existing unrelated fixed-clock edit retains stale_local. The hosted log does not include its observed refusal code."
  "2026-11-24T20:51:54.595Z",codex-agent,"The new linked command passed via pinned pm test. The two pre-existing links were refused by the runner because their provenance belongs to a different branch. Their selectors plus the new recovery and CLI checks passed directly under Node 22 and isolated Git configuration: 5 of 5. Existing links were preserved."
  "2026-11-24T21:57:01.060Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (CodeRabbit on resolution.ts): the retryable ado_partial_apply classification checked only ado_sync_base, so a peer's matching agreement followed by a local title edit was also reported as retryable. It now requires an agreement-only conflict (every conflicting field is one of ado_sync_base, ado_rev, ado_sync_intent); a mixed conflict keeps its previous classification. New test 'resolution recovery keeps a peer agreement followed by a local edit classified as stale_local' fails when the restriction is removed; the matching-agreement test still passes."
  "2026-11-24T23:26:43.017Z",codex-agent,"Review PRRT_kwDOUMUq1867oyUQ: reproduce the agreement write race after the full native head check succeeds, and verify that a peer title change stays stale_local."
  "2026-11-24T23:29:34.628Z",codex-agent,"Review PRRT_kwDOUMUq1867oyUQ: NativeWriteFence.update can throw a conflict projected to agreement fields after the full fence check. Resolution now rechecks the complete native history delta and allows retry only for a matching agreement-only conflict. The regression interleaves replay and a title edit at update entry. On f34a271 it reports ado_partial_apply instead of stale_local. With the fix it reports stale_local, preserves the title, and records one PATCH. Both existing agreement race tests pass."
  "2026-11-24T23:31:33.378Z",codex-agent,Daily Release run 45408908701 failed at Run release checks on resolution recovery serializes two writers using the same prepared decision. The runner rejected the observed refusal code in that test. The focused late-writer regression passed through pm test (1 of 1).
